# Ordered source patch series applied to the pinned upstream Pi tree, one filename per line.
#
# Order is this file's order and nothing else. Blank lines and `#` comments are ignored; a patch file
# in this directory that no line names is drift and fails preparation. Names must look like
# `NNNN-short-description.patch`.
#
# These six patches do not commute: 0002, 0003 and 0005 all change `packages/tui/src/{terminal,tui,index}.ts`,
# 0001, 0003, 0004 and 0005 all change `packages/coding-agent/src/{index.ts,core/extensions/*,modes/interactive/
# interactive-mode.ts}`, 0004 also changes seam A's own `core/native-submission.ts`, and 0002 and 0005 both
# change `packages/tui/src/{native-attachment,stdin-buffer}.ts`. 0002, 0003 and 0004 are the serialized forms
# regenerated against this order, so preparation applies them with no fuzz and no three-way fallback.
# Reordering this list breaks the preparation; regenerate the later patches instead.
#
# 0005 was taken directly after 0003, before 0004 existed in any series, and it still applies here unchanged:
# its `index.ts` and `interactive-mode.ts` hunks touch neither the export block nor the session and refusal
# regions 0004 rewrites, so `git apply --check --index --whitespace=error` accepts it at this position with no
# fuzz. It is therefore carried byte for byte rather than regenerated. 0005 depends on 0002 and 0003 and not on
# 0004; 0004 depends on 0001 and does not depend on 0005.
#
# 0006 is the native consumer-capability patch: the published input target in `packages/tui/src/{native-attachment,
# terminal,index}.ts`, the `dcs-pi-native-present-v1` codec in the new `packages/tui/src/native-present-markers.ts`
# with the ordered bracket in `{native-presentation,tui}.ts`, and bootstrap protocol 2 in
# `packages/coding-agent/src/core/{native-bootstrap,native-presentation}.ts`. It is generated against the tree
# 0001-0005 leave behind and applies only at this position; it is last because every file it touches is a file
# an earlier patch already rewrote.
#
# 0007 carries the processed-input provenance to the public input listener, and nothing else. `handleTerminalInput`
# has held the parsed sequence's `NativeInputProvenance` since 0002, but it was a local parameter: the only public
# carrier was `authorizeReturn`, which fires for a Return key alone. So an out-of-process host could see the origin
# of a Return and of nothing else, and a host-recognised gesture on any other key had no way to tell a single-origin
# sequence from one native framing assembled out of two attachments' bytes. This widens `TuiInputListener` with an
# OPTIONAL second parameter and passes the provenance already in scope at the single call site. It is additive and
# backward compatible: a one-argument listener is unchanged, and the type keeps accepting one. It adds no seam, no
# registration and no new decision point. Generated against the tree 0001-0006 leave behind, and last because
# `packages/tui/src/tui.ts` is a file 0002, 0003 and 0006 already rewrote.
